James inquired about potential breach of contract regarding a solar installation that remained unfinished for nearly a year, despite an estimated six-month timeline. Arachne outlined contract-law principles, emphasizing that “estimated” deadlines are often not binding. Acknowledging the delay as possibly unreasonable, she advised James to gather documentation and communicate with the contractor. Arachne suggested drafting a clear email requesting a completion timeline, followed by a formal notice of delay if necessary. She also provided recommendations for leveraging state resources and emphasized when to consult a lawyer. Finally, she noted practical steps for switching contractors if deadlines are ignored, including obtaining relevant project documents.
